  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "Comparative study of four quantum supervised-learning models (VQC, QSVC, EQNN, SQNN) for credit-card fraud detection on the standard 'creditcard.csv' European dataset (284,807 transactions, 492 fraud, 0.172% positive class). Features are angle-encoded into quantum states and processed by parameterized variational quantum circuits in a QGNN-style pipeline (GraphSAGE-style aggregation on the classical side, PennyLane for the quantum circuits, PyTorch for classical layers). Evaluation metrics: accuracy, precision, recall, F1. QSVC achieves the best balance (acc 91.3%, prec 92.6%, recall 86.1%, F1 89.2%); VQC second (acc 89.2%, F1 82.8%); EQNN third (acc 84.0%, F1 77.4%); SQNN worst (acc 73.0%, F1 71.3%). No explicit classical (non-quantum) baseline numerical comparison is reported. Execution is on simulator (PennyLane); no QPU, no specified qubit count, no noise model.",
